WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.270
On Friday a voice note

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.510
reached our staff group.

3
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.590
It sounded exactly like our head

4
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.970
teacher, asking me to send airtime

5
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.690
to a new number, urgently.

6
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.330
It wasn't him.

7
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.000
Today: how AI fakes voices,

8
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.000
faces and messages, and a simple

9
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.440
routine that beats them.

10
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.870
AI has made fakes cheap.

11
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.600
A short clip of someone's voice,

12
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.440
from a video or a voice note, can

13
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.680
be enough to copy it.

14
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.520
Photos can have faces swapped in.

15
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.960
And scam messages now come with

16
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.220
perfect spelling, in any language.

17
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.050
So the old warning signs are fading.

18
00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.330
Spelling mistakes, robotic voices,

19
00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.510
strange hands in pictures: each new

20
00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.910
tool fixes some of them.

21
00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.110
Hunting for glitches is a

22
00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.270
race you will lose.

23
00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.510
What does work is a routine.

24
00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.300
Pause, because urgency is the trick.

25
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.790
Check on a channel you already trust:

26
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.930
call back on the number you saved,

27
00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.370
not the one in the message.

28
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.220
And agree a code word for

29
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.360
anything about money.

30
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.780
Here's how it plays out.

31
00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.310
The fake asks for airtime.

32
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.120
You don't reply in that chat.

33
00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.950
You call the head teacher on his saved

34
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.970
number, and he says: that wasn't me.

35
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:25.640
Quick check!

36
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.860
A voice note from a new number

37
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.500
sounds just like my sister.

38
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.590
She says she's stuck and needs money now.

39
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.240
What do I do first?

40
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.160
Call her back on the number you saved.

41
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.590
A reply in that chat goes

42
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.850
straight to the scammer.

43
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.440
If you can't reach her, ask for

44
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.780
your family's code word,

45
00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.880
something a fake couldn't know.

46
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.080
Fakes also hurt people at school.

47
00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.120
A made-up picture of a pupil or

48
00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.120
a teacher can spread through a

49
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.380
class group in minutes.

50
00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.830
If it happens: care for the person first,

51
00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.230
don't forward it, note where it is, and

52
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.750
report it to the head teacher.

53
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.480
With my pupils, I'm clear: making a fake

54
00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.920
of a real person is never a joke.

55
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.990
It can break the law, and it

56
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.310
always hurts someone.

57
00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.490
In the app, take a phone call from “IT

58
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.270
support” that needs your code.

59
00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.770
Answer the way many people would, then

60
00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.930
take the call again and spot the

61
00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.370
tricks: authority, hurry and fear.

62
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.160
Your turn.

63
00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.350
A video of our head teacher saying school

64
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:38.190
is closed tomorrow is going round.

65
00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.750
It looks real.

66
00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.940
What's the best check?

67
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.570
Check the school's usual channel: a real

68
00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:46.810
announcement will be there too.

69
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.030
Remember: fakes are cheap and

70
00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.350
glitches don't last.

71
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.000
Pause, call back, and use a code word.

72
00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.530
And never forward a fake.

73
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.110
Try it in class tomorrow:

74
00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.170
play “Pause and check”.

75
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.900
Read out a pretend urgent message

76
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.260
from someone the class knows.

77
00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.910
Pupils say what they would do, and the

78
00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.550
class agrees one way to check, like

79
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.410
calling back or a family code word.
